[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known as one issue. It is three. Of the 412 unique
reports merged into it, the table below counts how many belong to each cause.

<Callout>
Not known. One fix is queued; two other problems have no ticket of their own.
</Callout>

## What #4471 really holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

1. **Parser, 374 reports.** The shared parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get flipped dates. This is the bug #4471 describes.
2. **Form hint, 33 reports.** `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People on day-first tenants type month first, and the form reads it their way. Intake tagged these `parser`; the tenant and form say otherwise.
3. **One-day move, 5 reports.** The date is one day off, not flipped (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620). The desk's notes list them, but the cause counts them under `parser`. Likely a time zone or date-boundary problem; not confirmed.

## Why the merge hid this

Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. These reports share
subjects such as "Wrong day on the invite" while their causes differ. The export also repeats 15 report
ids; count each id once.

## Tickets

One GitHub issue per problem, in `Lstanislao/what-it-shows-s01e03`: #1 parser, #2 form hint, #3 one-day move.

